# Initramfs manifest
#
# `cargo xtask image` reads this to decide which files go into the initial
# ramdisk. It is a manifest rather than a directory scan for one reason: a build
# must be reproducible, and a scan picks up whatever happens to be in the build
# directory, including stale artifacts from a previous configuration.
#
# Format: one path per line, relative to the repository root. Lines beginning
# with `#` are comments. There is no globbing yet; M2 adds it when there is more
# than one binary to place.
#
# # Why this file is empty
#
# NovaOS v0.1.0 (M0) has no userspace. The kernel is the only thing on the ISO,
# and `module_path` in `limine.conf` points at a file this build does not create.
# That is deliberate: Limine treats a *missing module file* differently from a
# missing kernel, and leaving the line in place means the M2 change is one line
# here plus the userspace landing in the image, not a change to the boot contract
# that the kernel already depends on.

# (no entries yet — userspace arrives in M2)